        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Incline is the one upgrade on this format worth paying real money for.
            <strong class="text-white">At 3 mph, 10% grade more than doubles the work without
            walking any faster</strong> — it is what takes a walking pad from accumulating steps to
            producing genuine training.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Find out whether the incline is fixed, manual or powered before comparing maximum grades,
            check the deck thickness against
            <a href="/treadmill-desk/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">your desk height</a>,
            and do not hold the rail. If the pad is purely for desk work, skip incline and buy deck
            length and a low
            <a href="/walking-pad/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">minimum speed</a>
            instead.
          </p>
